# Three vars, no more. All optional in dev (defaults match a standard local setup).
#
# ── VITE_PLATFORM_BASE_URL ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base path the frontend uses for platform API calls.
# Keep this as /api — it MUST stay relative so calls stay same-origin.
# - Dev  : Vite forwards `/api/*` to http://localhost:8080 (hardcoded in vite.config.ts).
# - Prod : `vercel.json` rewrites `/api/*` to the deployed platform URL.
# Absolute values would force the refresh cookie down to SameSite=None,
# which platform's RefreshCookieService forbids. Do not change.
VITE_PLATFORM_BASE_URL=/api

# ── VITE_AGENT_BASE_URL ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Absolute origin of agent-system, e.g. https://agent.example.com
# Leave UNSET for local dev (falls back to `/agent`, Vite proxies to
# http://localhost:8000). On Vercel, set to the agent-system HTTPS origin —
# NO `/agent` suffix, no trailing slash. Setting it makes agent calls
# cross-origin, which needs `CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS=<this frontend's origin>`
# on agent-system. See vercel.md for the split-origin design.
# VITE_AGENT_BASE_URL=

# ── VITE_MODE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `dev` gates dev-only UI (Dev nav item, debug pages). Anything else hides them.
VITE_MODE=dev
